1. download python
2. install ffmpeg
    https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/
    download ffmpeg-release-essentials.zip
    extract zip

     Add it to your PATH
    This is the step people usually get stuck on. PATH is just a list of folders Windows checks whenever you type a command, so it knows where to find the program.

    Press the Windows key, type "environment variables", and click "Edit the system environment variables"
    In the window that opens, click the "Environment Variables..." button near the bottom
    In the bottom section ("System variables"), find and select the row named Path, then click Edit
    Click New, and paste in the exact path to the bin folder inside your extracted ffmpeg folder, e.g.:
    C:\ffmpeg\ffmpeg-7.x-essentials_build\bin

    Verify it worked
    Close any open terminal/PowerShell windows completely (this matters — PATH changes don't apply to terminals that were already open) and open a fresh one. Then type:

    ffmpeg -version
3. install pyaudio type in terminal:
    py -m pip install pyaudio

4. install python packages (requirements.txt)
    pip install -r requirements.txt

5. environment values
    open new terminal:
    setx OPENAI_API_KEY "sk-your-key-here"
    setx AZURE_SPEECH_KEY "your-azure-key-here"
    setx AZURE_SPEECH_REGION "eastus" 

    if successful, close and reopen terminal and 
    verify success:
    echo $env:OPENAI_API_KEY

6. run code
    cd into Shifts-and-Giggles
    python talk.py